// THE HOLE'S OWN CELL DECIDES — not a copy of its type.
//
// none_of returns Option(a) and the hole wants Option(Int): the SAME type
// under unification, two different shapes under a structural comparison. So
// this fixture measures which one the proposer uses. The vocabulary used to
// ask a hand-rolled name-and-shape match standing in for the union-find the
// medium already owns, and it answered NO — a proven survivor was never
// offered, and the medium asked a question it could have answered.
//
// The same read fixes a defect that had always been here and could not be
// seen: None was minted as None(), a zero-arg application of something that
// is not a function. It was ill-typed by construction, its mismatch leaked
// out of the candidate's own judgment to a span in an unrelated module, and
// the candidate still rendered as a bare ?? — a foreign error beside a
// proposal that was never admissible. With the hole a real cell the refusal
// became visible, and a nullary constructor is now the value it is.
//
// Contract at the hole: the fill is none_of() with its Why, or None beside
// it — never a bare ?? and never a diagnostic from a module nobody opened.

fn none_of() -> Option(a) with Pure = None

fn opt() -> Option(Int) with Pure = ??

fn main() = match opt() {
  Some(n) => n,
  None => 0,
}
